1321	\begin{theorem}[Idempotent generator of the \(k[X]\)-diagonal ideal]
1322	  \label{thm:exists_idempotent_lift}
1323	  \lean{AlgebraicJacobian.Diagonal.exists_idempotent_lift}
1324	  \uses{def:diagonalSetup}
1325	  \leanok
1326	  Suppose \(k[X] \to B\) is formally unramified and essentially of finite type. Then the
1327	  \(k[X]\)-diagonal ideal \(\ker \mu_{k[X]}\) is generated by an idempotent element, and this
1328	  idempotent is \(\pi(\mathrm{elift})\) for some lift \(\mathrm{elift} \in B \otimes_k B\):
1329	  \[
1330	    \ker \mu_{k[X]} \;=\; (\pi\,\mathrm{elift}), \qquad (\pi\,\mathrm{elift})^2 = \pi\,\mathrm{elift}.
